{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Multi-Object Tracking & Video Memory Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: IoU-based cost matrix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bbox_iou(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    a, b: (N, 4) arrays of [x1, y1, x2, y2]."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Returns (N_a, N_b) IoU matrix."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ax1, ay1, ax2, ay2 = a[:, 0], a[:, 1], a[:, 2], a[:, 3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bx1, by1, bx2, by2 = b[:, 0], b[:, 1], b[:, 2], b[:, 3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_x1 = np.maximum(ax1[:, None], bx1[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_y1 = np.maximum(ay1[:, None], by1[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_x2 = np.minimum(ax2[:, None], bx2[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_y2 = np.minimum(ay2[:, None], by2[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter = np.clip(inter_x2 - inter_x1, 0, None) * np.clip(inter_y2 - inter_y1, 0, None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    area_a = (ax2 - ax1) * (ay2 - ay1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    area_b = (bx2 - bx1) * (by2 - by1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    union = area_a[:, None] + area_b[None, :] - inter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return inter / np.clip(union, 1e-8, None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Minimal SORT-style tracker"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Fixed constant-velocity Kalman omitted for brevity \u2014 we use a simple IoU association here; in production the Kalman predict is essential. The `sort` Python package provides the full version."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Track:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, tid, bbox, frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.id = tid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bbox = bbox"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.last_frame = frame"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.hits = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def update(self, bbox, frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bbox = bbox"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.last_frame = frame"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.hits += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SimpleTracker:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, iou_threshold=0.3, max_age=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.tracks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.next_id = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.iou_threshold = iou_threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_age = max_age"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def step(self, detections, frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not self.tracks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for d in detections:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.tracks.append(Track(self.next_id, d, frame))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.next_id += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return [(t.id, t.bbox) for t in self.tracks]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        track_boxes = np.array([t.bbox for t in self.tracks])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        det_boxes = np.array(detections) if len(detections) else np.empty((0, 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        iou = bbox_iou(track_boxes, det_boxes) if len(det_boxes) else np.zeros((len(track_boxes), 0))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cost = 1 - iou"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cost[iou < self.iou_threshold] = 1e6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        matched_track = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        matched_det = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if cost.size > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            row, col = linear_sum_assignment(cost)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for r, c in zip(row, col):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if cost[r, c] < 1.0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    self.tracks[r].update(det_boxes[c], frame)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    matched_track.add(r); matched_det.add(c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, d in enumerate(det_boxes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if i not in matched_det:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.tracks.append(Track(self.next_id, d, frame))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.next_id += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.tracks = [t for t in self.tracks if frame - t.last_frame <= self.max_age]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [(t.id, t.bbox) for t in self.tracks]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "60 lines. Takes per-frame detections, returns per-frame track IDs. Real systems add the Kalman predict, ByteTrack's second-stage re-match, and appearance features."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Synthetic trajectory test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_frames(num_frames=20, num_objects=3, H=240, W=320, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    starts = rng.uniform(20, 200, size=(num_objects, 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    velocities = rng.uniform(-5, 5, size=(num_objects, 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    frames = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for f in range(num_frames):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dets = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(num_objects):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            cx, cy = starts[i] + f * velocities[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            dets.append([cx - 10, cy - 10, cx + 10, cy + 10])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        frames.append(dets)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return frames"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tracker = SimpleTracker()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for f, dets in enumerate(synthetic_frames()):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tracks = tracker.step(dets, f)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three objects moving in straight lines should keep their IDs across all 20 frames."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: ID-switch metric"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def count_id_switches(tracks_per_frame, gt_per_frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tracks_per_frame:  list of list of (track_id, bbox)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gt_per_frame:      list of list of (gt_id, bbox)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Returns number of ID switches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prev_assignment = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    switches = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for tracks, gts in zip(tracks_per_frame, gt_per_frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not tracks or not gts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_boxes = np.array([b for _, b in tracks])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        g_boxes = np.array([b for _, b in gts])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        iou = bbox_iou(g_boxes, t_boxes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for g_idx, (gt_id, _) in enumerate(gts):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            j = iou[g_idx].argmax()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if iou[g_idx, j] > 0.5:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                t_id = tracks[j][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if gt_id in prev_assignment and prev_assignment[gt_id] != t_id:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    switches += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                prev_assignment[gt_id] = t_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return switches"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is a simplified IDF1-adjacent metric: count how many times a ground-truth object changes its assigned predicted track ID. Real MOTA / IDF1 / HOTA tooling lives in `py-motmetrics` and `TrackEval`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Run the synthetic tracker above with 3, 10, and 30 objects. Report ID-switch count in each case. Identify where the simple IoU-only association starts to fail.\n2. **(Medium)** Add a constant-velocity Kalman predict step before association. Show that short (2-3 frame) occlusions no longer cause ID switches.\n3. **(Hard)** Integrate SAM 2's memory-based tracker (via `transformers`) as an alternative tracker backend. Run both SimpleTracker and SAM 2 on a 30-second clip of a crowd and compare ID-switch counts, manually labelling ground-truth IDs for 5 salient people."
      ]
    }
